# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to each machine's
# core.autocrlf. Without this file the working tree's endings depend on who
# checked it out: this repo is developed on Windows (autocrlf=true, so CRLF)
# and on macOS (LF), which is how `src/routes/region-selector/+page.svelte`
# ended up with 135 CRLF lines and 27 LF ones in the same file. Git normalises
# on commit, so `git diff` reports nothing while every commit prints a wall of
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings and a whole-file rewrite hides in the
# next diff.
#
# LF in the repository and LF in the working tree, on every platform. The tree
# holds no shell scripts or .bat/.cmd files, so nothing here needs CRLF to
# stay executable; CI runs on macOS and Linux, where LF is what the toolchain
# expects anyway.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never normalise, never diff as text. A newline "fixed" inside
# a PNG or an icon corrupts it silently.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
